snp5.18:4.1 starts: They went to the Awakened One,
snp5.18:4.2 starts: consummate in conduct, the seer.
snp5.18:4.3 starts: They went to the excellent Awakened One,
snp5.18:4.4 starts: asking subtle questions.
snp5.18:7.1 starts: Whoever would practice
snp5.18:7.2 starts: as the Awakened One taught
snp5.18:7.3 starts: concerning each of these questions,
snp5.18:7.4 starts: would go from the near shore to the
snp5.18:8.1 starts: would go from the near shore to the
snp5.18:8.2 starts: developing the path supreme.
snp5.18:8.3 starts: The path is for going beyond,
snp5.18:8.4 starts: and so it’s called “To the Far Shore.”
snp5.11:4.1 starts: Those knowing this, mindful,
snp5.11:4.2 starts: fully unbound
snp5.11:4.3 starts: don’t serve as Māra’s servants,
snp5.11:4.4 starts: don’t come under Māra’s sway.
snp5.12:3.1 starts: The Buddha:
snp5.12:3.3 starts: & see renunciation as rest.
snp5.12:3.4 starts: Let there be nothing grasped
snp5.12:3.5 starts: or rejected by you.
snp5.13:1.1 starts: I entreat the one who has
snp5.13:1.3 starts: abandoned delight—crossed over the flood, released;
snp5.13:1.4 starts: abandoned theory—very intelligent:
snp5.13:1.5 starts: Having heard the Nāga, they will leave—
snp5.13:2.1 starts: the many gathered
# superseded: snp5.13:2.2 starts: hero,
snp5.13:2.3 starts: So tell them, please,
snp5.13:2.4 starts: how this Dhamma has
snp5.13:4.1 starts: So a monk, mindful,
snp5.13:4.2 starts: seeing these people
snp5.13:4.3 starts: as entangled in Death’s realm,
snp5.13:4.4 starts: should cling to nothing
snp5.15:2.1 starts: I ask the Sakyan about the knowledge
snp5.15:2.2 starts: of one devoid of perception of forms,
snp5.15:2.3 starts: who has abandoned all the body,
snp5.15:2.4 starts: who sees, within & without,
snp5.15:2.5 starts: ‘There is nothing’:
snp5.15:2.6 starts: How is he
snp5.15:4.1 starts: Knowing directly
snp5.15:4.2 starts: the origin of nothingness
snp5.15:4.3 starts: to be the fetter of delight,
snp5.15:4.4 starts: one then sees there
snp5.15:4.5 starts: That’s his genuine knowledge—
snp5.15:4.6 starts: the brahman who has lived
snp5.16:1.1 starts: Twice now, Sakyan,
snp5.16:1.3 starts: but you, One with Eyes,
snp5.16:1.4 starts: “When asked the third time,
snp5.16:1.5 starts: So I have heard.
snp5.16:4.1 starts: The Buddha:
snp5.16:4.2 starts: regard the world as
snp5.16:4.3 starts: having removed any view
snp5.16:4.4 starts: This way
snp5.16:4.5 starts: One who regards the world
snp5.16:4.6 starts: isn’t seen by Death’s King.
snp5.18:5.1 starts: The Awakened One,
snp5.18:5.2 starts: answered in line with the truth.
snp5.18:5.3 starts: By answering their questions, the sage
snp5.18:5.4 starts: delighted the brahmans.
snp5.19:2.1 starts: His delusion & stains
snp5.19:2.2 starts: left behind; left behind,
snp5.19:2.3 starts: his hypocrisy, conceit:
snp5.19:2.4 starts: Let me praise his beautiful words.
snp5.19:8.1 starts: Bāvarī:
snp5.19:8.2 starts: can you stay apart from him—
snp5.19:8.3 starts: Gotama of deep knowledge,
snp5.19:8.4 starts: Gotama of deep intelligence,
snp5.19:10.1 starts: Ven. Piṅgiya:
snp5.19:10.2 starts: can I stay apart from him—
snp5.19:10.3 starts: Gotama of deep knowledge,
snp5.19:10.4 starts: Gotama of deep intelligence,
snp5.19:13.1 starts: My conviction, rapture,
snp5.19:13.2 starts: don’t stray from Gotama’s message.
snp5.19:13.3 starts: To whatever direction he goes,
snp5.19:13.4 starts: to that direction I bow down.
